1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,058
Excuse me. Can you help me?

2
00:00:04,058 --> 00:00:05,778
Sure, what do you want?

3
00:00:05,778 --> 00:00:07,956
Where is 83 Wooster Street?

4
00:00:07,956 --> 00:00:11,912
That's easy. Walk to the corner.

5
00:00:11,912 --> 00:00:13,762
Then make a left turn.

6
00:00:13,762 --> 00:00:17,250
Then walk two blocks to the traffic light.

7
00:00:17,250 --> 00:00:17,868
Make another left to Wooster.

8
00:00:17,868 --> 00:00:18,761
Thank you.

9
00:00:18,761 --> 00:00:21,596
To the corner and then a left?

10
00:00:21,596 --> 00:00:22,646
Yeah. A left.

11
00:00:22,646 --> 00:00:25,324
Hot dog? Only seventy-five cents.

12
00:00:25,324 --> 00:00:39,381
No. Thank you. I have a dinner date.

13
00:00:39,381 --> 00:00:44,669
555-9470...and it's busy....

14
00:00:44,669 --> 00:00:45,669
Try again.

15
00:00:45,669 --> 00:00:50,047
555-9470...and it's still busy.

16
00:00:50,047 --> 00:01:01,059
Excuse me, ma'am.

17
00:01:01,059 --> 00:01:05,515
I'm looking for 83 Wooster Street.

18
00:01:05,515 --> 00:01:16,342
Yes. Wooster Street is two blocks,

19
00:01:16,342 --> 00:01:21,405
and 83 is to the right, about two houses.

20
00:01:21,405 --> 00:01:23,383
Thank you, thank you!

21
00:01:23,383 --> 00:01:24,240
You're welcome.

22
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:25,526
Who is it?

23
00:01:25,526 --> 00:01:29,739
Harry Bennett. Is this Susan?

24
00:01:29,739 --> 00:01:32,717
Yes, it is. Come up.

25
00:01:32,717 --> 00:02:05,074
I'm on the top floor.

26
00:02:05,074 --> 00:02:07,741
Hello, Harry. It's nice to meet you.

27
00:02:07,741 --> 00:02:09,385
Nice to meet you, Susan.

28
00:02:09,385 --> 00:02:11,441
Sorry I'm late.

29
00:02:11,441 --> 00:02:14,408
The traffic. The parking. I was lost.

30
00:02:14,408 --> 00:02:16,986
What pretty flowers! Thank you.

31
00:02:16,986 --> 00:02:18,933
Oh, please come in.

32
00:02:18,933 --> 00:02:23,542
Don't worry about being late. It's fine.

33
00:02:23,542 --> 00:02:27,420
Excuse the mess. I just moved here.

34
00:02:27,420 --> 00:02:33,162
Oh, I'd like you to meet my sister-in-law Marilyn.

35
00:02:33,162 --> 00:02:35,521
Marilyn Stewart, this is Harry Bennett.

36
00:02:35,521 --> 00:02:37,521
Pleased to meet you.

37
00:02:37,521 --> 00:02:40,643
Nice to meet you, Harry.

38
00:02:40,643 --> 00:02:42,010
Are we too late for our dinner reservation?

39
00:02:42,010 --> 00:02:44,538
No, the restaurant will hold our table.

40
00:02:44,538 --> 00:02:46,766
I know the owner very well.

41
00:02:46,766 --> 00:02:47,779
I eat there a lot.

42
00:02:47,779 --> 00:02:49,603
Do you know the phone number of the restaurant?

43
00:02:49,603 --> 00:02:50,633
I'd like to call home

44
00:02:50,633 --> 00:02:52,955
and leave the number with the baby-sitter.

45
00:02:52,955 --> 00:02:55,049
Sure. The number is... five five five...seventeen twenty.

46
00:02:55,049 --> 00:02:57,567
May I use the phone?

47
00:02:57,567 --> 00:03:16,545
Five five five...one seven two oh. Hello?

48
00:03:16,545 --> 00:03:22,501
Hi, Michelle. It's Daddy.

49
00:03:22,501 --> 00:03:24,945
Can I speak to Betty?

50
00:03:24,945 --> 00:03:28,457
I want to leave the phone number of the restaurant...

51
00:03:28,457 --> 00:03:34,413
Hi, Betty. I'll be at five five five...seventeen twenty.

52
00:03:34,413 --> 00:03:40,369
OK. Thanks. See you later.

53
00:03:40,369 --> 00:03:43,347
Well, that's done. Shall we go?

54
00:03:43,347 --> 00:03:45,347
I'm ready. See you later, Marilyn.

55
00:03:45,347 --> 00:03:46,325
Have a nice evening.

56
00:03:46,325 --> 00:03:48,745
Bye, Marilyn. Hope to see you again.

57
00:03:48,745 --> 00:03:50,636
Me, too. Have fun!

58
00:03:50,636 --> 00:03:55,259
Thanks.

59
00:03:55,259 --> 00:03:57,259
After you.
